                                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[I finally found a Google Photos alternative worth switching to]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/i-finally-found-google-photos-alternative-worth-switching-to/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Rahul Naskar]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/torn-google-photos-logo-revealing-the-immich-icon-in-the-middle.png" length="1171" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[google photos]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google]]></category><category><![CDATA[Utilities]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google Photos]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            It gave me something Google Photos never could
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>I prefer to live in the moment rather than behind a lens, but I don't shy away from capturing moments that I want to stay with me forever. I trust my Samsung Galaxy phone and Google Photos to make this easy for me.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:15:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/i-finally-found-google-photos-alternative-worth-switching-to/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[I was drowning in Galaxy notification spam until I turned on this one hidden feature]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/i-was-drowning-galaxy-notification-spam-until-i-turned-on-one-hidden-feature/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Jade Bryan Jardinico]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/hand-holding-a-galaxy-phone-displaying-notification-settings-with-bell-icons-around-it.jpg" length="438" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[notification channels]]></category><category><![CDATA[One UI 8]]></category><category><![CDATA[Operating Systems]]></category><category><![CDATA[notification channels]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            Notification Categories is a critical tool in reclaiming my Android notifications panel
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>I love One UI on my <a href="https://www.androidpolice.com/samsung-galaxy-z-flip-7-review/" target="_blank">Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7</a>. It always feels just as cohesive as the stock Android experience on my Google Pixel phone.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 13:30:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/i-was-drowning-galaxy-notification-spam-until-i-turned-on-one-hidden-feature/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[I installed the top 10 productivity apps on my Google Pixel, but only 4 were genuinely useful]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/installed-10-productivity-apps-on-google-pixel-only-4-were-useful/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Parth Shah]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/pixel-9-pro-home-screen-launcher-app-icons.jpg" length="4082" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[Android Apps]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google Pixel]]></category><category><![CDATA[Productivity]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android Apps]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google Pixel]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            Most apps failed my real-world test
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>The Google Play Store is packed with productivity apps promising to organize my tasks, sharpen my focus, and transform the way I work.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:30:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/installed-10-productivity-apps-on-google-pixel-only-4-were-useful/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[I saved gigabytes of Google storage by fixing a mistake I didn't know I was making]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/i-saved-gigabytes-of-google-storage-by-fixing-a-mistake-i-didnt-know-i-was-making/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Jon Gilbert]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/hand-holding-a-phone-showing-google-one-storage-usage.png" length="695" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[google photos]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google]]></category><category><![CDATA[Best Reads]]></category><category><![CDATA[Utilities]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google Photos]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android Police's Best Reads]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            Google is probably duplicating your data
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>By the end of August 2026, all Android backups will count towards your Google account's storage quota. If your account's storage is full, your Android phone will stop backing up until space is freed.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:15:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/i-saved-gigabytes-of-google-storage-by-fixing-a-mistake-i-didnt-know-i-was-making/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[The first thing I do for friends switching from iPhone to Android is change this setting]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/setting-iphone-switchers-should-change/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Ben Khalesi]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/a-hand-using-gesture-navigation-on-a-google-pixel.png" length="1100" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[Android]]></category><category><![CDATA[ios]]></category><category><![CDATA[Operating Systems]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android]]></category><category><![CDATA[iOS]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            This is why switching OS feels like starting over
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>Whenever a friend texts me that they have switched from an iPhone to an Android phone, I offer to help set it up.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:00:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/setting-iphone-switchers-should-change/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[Android's new backup trick is exactly what I needed, and here's how to turn it on]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/android-new-file-backup-trick/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Rita El Khoury]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/wm/2026/07/android-backups.jpg" length="286" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[backup]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android]]></category><category><![CDATA[documents]]></category><category><![CDATA[Operating Systems]]></category><category><![CDATA[backup]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android]]></category><category><![CDATA[documents]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            Google can automatically do it for me
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>Backups are the first thing I set up on any Android phone. Google Photos sync, system backups, and WhatsApp backups — these are the big three for me and for any family member, and they've saved us many a headache.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:00:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/android-new-file-backup-trick/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[I stopped trusting star ratings: Here's how I judge a place on Google Maps]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/stopped-trusting-star-ratings-how-i-judge-place-on-google-maps/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Anu Joy]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/a-google-maps-pin-surrounded-by-restaurant-reviews-and-star-ratings.png" length="608" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[Google Maps]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google]]></category><category><![CDATA[Best Reads]]></category><category><![CDATA[Utilities]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google Maps]]></category><category><![CDATA[Google]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android Police's Best Reads]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            It has become my go-to research tool
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>Whenever I'm planning to visit a new restaurant, café, attraction, or park, I rarely decide based on the name alone. A place can have a high rating, but that doesn't always tell the full story.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:00:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/stopped-trusting-star-ratings-how-i-judge-place-on-google-maps/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[My favorite Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8 upgrade finally lets the clamshell take on Apple]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/my-favorite-galaxy-z-flip-8-upgrade-is-all-about-the-cover/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Tom Bedford]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/wm/2026/07/samsung-galaxy-z-flip-8-home.jpg" length="1752" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8]]></category><category><![CDATA[Samsung]]></category><category><![CDATA[Samsung Galaxy Unpacked July 2026]]></category><category><![CDATA[Phones]]></category><category><![CDATA[Samsung]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            Making the smaller screen useful
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>To me, the most important part of any flip phone I use is the cover screen. That's not just a stance I take with clamshell foldable phones, but an important principle I maintained for my original LG flip phone two decades ago.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 10:00:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/my-favorite-galaxy-z-flip-8-upgrade-is-all-about-the-cover/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[I'm not letting Claude touch my passwords, no matter how safe Anthropic claims it is]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/claude-wants-my-passwords/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Irene Okpanachi]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/claude-password-security-illustration.png" length="144" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[Anthropic Claude]]></category><category><![CDATA[password management]]></category><category><![CDATA[Best Reads]]></category><category><![CDATA[Productivity]]></category><category><![CDATA[password management]]></category><category><![CDATA[Android Police's Best Reads]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            My passwords are mine
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>I've accepted that artificial intelligence is the future. What concerns me is how companies are turning my vulnerability into a product.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:00:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/claude-wants-my-passwords/</guid></item>                                                                <item><title><![CDATA[This display upgrade made me excited about Samsung's foldables again]]></title><link>https://www.androidpolice.com/this-display-upgrade-made-me-excited-about-samsungs-foldables-again/</link><dc:creator><![CDATA[Jon Gilbert]]></dc:creator><enclosure url="https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/two-views-of-a-samsung-galaxy-z-fold-8-ultra-shown-partially-open-and-fully-open.png" length="1903" type="image/jpeg"/><category><![CDATA[Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8]]></category><category><![CDATA[Samsung]]></category><category><![CDATA[Phones]]></category><category><![CDATA[Samsung]]></category><description><![CDATA[
                                            I'm finally considering a Samsung foldable
                                        ]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[
                                                                                                                                    <p>When choosing a new Android phone for my personal use, I give most specs only a cursory examination.</p>                    ]]></content:encoded><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:15:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.androidpolice.com/this-display-upgrade-made-me-excited-about-samsungs-foldables-again/</guid></item></channel>
